==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 7.33 seconds<sup>220f</sup>, delay 20~22 seconds<sup>600f~660f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~22 seconds<sup>600f~660f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bun Bun Black]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn, delay 40~66.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~2,000f</sup>.
**5 [[Dolphina]]s spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Kory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Never use erasers on this stage. Because of their 1 knockback, they usually survive Bun Bun's Attack and make Kory unleash a dangerous wave that wipes out your stack. Instead focus on using low health meatshields like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk]] or [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]]. They have low enough health to be knocked back by Bun Bun's attack therefore making Kory miss. [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] is also a great choice due to having Strong Against Bun Bun and being stackable. You can also use [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] to deal strong wave damage to Dolphinas.

If you have [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or any other Wave Blockers, bring them. They completely destroy this stage by preventing Kory from making Wave Attacks and removing all of the threat that he posed.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] (i.e. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus]], [[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Costumed Witchy Neneko]], [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]], etc.) - Breaks this stage by blocking Kory's Wave attacks making it not threatening.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk]]/[[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Glittering Macho]] - Breaks this stage, but in an entirely different way from Wave Shields. They are spammable meatshields with Wave Immunity, meaning that even if Kory ''does'' release a wave, it won't even destroy your frontlines. Paired with Wave Immune attackers, they make this stage a joke.
*Cat Clones (i.e. [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie]], etc.) - Better meatshields than Erasers for this stage because of their knockbacks and low health causing Kory to miss.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - Has massive damage against Kory and immunity to his waves. Plus, he also has pretty quick speed to get into the Dolphina's blind spot, and can intercept their attacks easily.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - Good and stackable midranger that is able to deal good damage to Bun Bun and Kory.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] - Good pick to damage Dolphinas with its powerfull wave attack.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - Decent pick against Bun Bun because of its Massive Damage versus Black.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]] - Good pick against Kory that can create knockback surges to push Kory away.
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying]] - If you build up a push to the base along with Bombercat and wave blockers such as Octopus, its mini wave will render the Dolphinas and Kory useless and shred them if they manage to get closer.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Iz]] - Massive damage against Traitless allows it to demolish Kory and Dolphinas without any effort.

==Trivia==
*A boudoir is a woman's private dressing room or bedroom.
*In Middle English, "lamb" could refer to a Christian believer. Since it's in [[Heaven's Back Alley]], that may be what the "Lamb" in this stage's name refers to.

